{"title":"2018 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many positive integer factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/5/66560809e37ebbea3f553d39a5eac472f6fe1b54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36,000,000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"88\" height=\"16\" /> are not perfect squares?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can use <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Complementary_counting\" title=\"Complementary counting\">complementary counting</a>. Taking the prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/5/66560809e37ebbea3f553d39a5eac472f6fe1b54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36,000,000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"88\" height=\"16\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/f/67f1be03e83f6a56ff3d25f61ca04da96432dcc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^8\\cdot3^2\\cdot5^6$\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />.So the total number of factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/5/66560809e37ebbea3f553d39a5eac472f6fe1b54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36,000,000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"88\" height=\"16\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/6/e36e66f47c9aaa433173a9cb197b0d586b083343.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(8+1)(2+1)(6+1) = 189$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"214\" height=\"18\" /> factors. Now we need to find the number of factors that are perfect squares. So back to the prime factorization, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/6/226100f3cb1e251b4b80b52543e950b8e100dade.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^8\\cdot3^2\\cdot5^6 = 4^4\\cdot9^1\\cdot5^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"174\" height=\"15\" />. Now we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/e/14e7d400e1a0c40f10c0a7b266a9d7ed31f1c5fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4+1)(1+1)(3+1)=40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"205\" height=\"18\" /> factors that are perfect squares. So there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/2/dc2bb6769bf6d5dc5ff3c9b4e54da7a8c31d7582.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$189-40=\\boxed{149}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"23\" /> positive integer factors that are not perfect squares.\n</p><p>~Ultraman\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNCO_Math_Contest_II\" title=\"2018 UNCO Math Contest II\">2018 UNCO Math Contest II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems\" title=\"2018 UNCO Math Contest II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2018 UNCO Math Contest II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://uncmathcontest.wordpress.com/\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2018 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2018 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2018 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2018 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2018 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2018 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2018 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2018 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2018 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2018 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2018 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\